  "_why": "How far does the original get when spawned unattended, and where does the load driver's click die? One hook per screen entry point, so the tag alone says where it stalled -- no pointer-to-screen mapping needed. CChitin::AsynchronousUpdate proves the engine tick runs at all (its HITS count is the tick total; `max` only caps logging). The CNetwork/popup hooks cover every branch of CScreenConnection::OnLoadGameButtonClick (CScreenConnection.cpp:1212-1296): connection init -> HostNewSession -> CreatePlayer -> StartLoad, with SummonPopup as the failure exit.",
